  "latestMilestone": "Canonical SWIR_OS main now includes the verified native SWIR Calculator on top of the existing native PDF Viewer and Photo Studio foundations while the measurable roadmap remains 54/65 (83.1%). Calculator is a first-party unprivileged GTK4 application with a strict AST allowlist instead of Python eval/exec, bounded expression complexity, bounded exponent/result magnitude, fixed shell/image integration and dedicated Wayland plus Debian 13 runtime verification. It closes a real Product Baseline utility gap but does not complete the broader essential native daily-use application suite roadmap deliverable, so roadmap progress is intentionally unchanged. Physical Live USB qualification remains pending; Secure Boot and legacy BIOS are not claimed.",
